  "instructions": "## Numbers that describe a shape\n\nA structure is a list of atom coordinates `[x, y, z]`. Two measures appear in every structure paper.\n\n1. `centroid(coords)`: the mean position.\n2. `radius_of_gyration(coords)`: sqrt of the mean squared distance of atoms from the centroid.\n3. `rmsd(a, b)`: for two structures with the same number of atoms in the same order, sqrt of the mean squared distance between corresponding atoms (no superposition here).\n4. `centre(coords)`: a new list with the centroid moved to the origin.",
